WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.267
The multi-agent system that loops forever.

2
00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:08.030
Fifteen percent of tasks never finish, and the token bill is exploding.

3
00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:10.167
Let's see why, and how to stop it.

4
00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:14.085
You built a researcher, writer, reviewer crew.

5
00:00:14.085 --> 00:00:15.267
It works in testing.

6
00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:18.967
In production, about fifteen percent of tasks never finish.

7
00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:22.200
And those runs cost twenty times the normal tokens.

8
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.367
Here's the loop.

9
00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:25.800
The writer drafts.

10
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:32.919
The reviewer finds something to improve, because an LLM is a generator of critique, not a threshold function.

11
00:00:32.919 --> 00:00:34.733
It can always find something.

12
00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:38.100
The writer revises, and nothing ever says acceptable.

13
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.867
Now add controls, in order of importance.

14
00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:45.733
A rubric with a pass threshold, so acceptable is computable.

15
00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:48.100
A hard cap of two revision rounds.

16
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.067
A token budget that aborts instead of burning money silently.

17
00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:55.033
A detector that stops when scores stop improving.

18
00:00:55.333 --> 00:00:59.108
And specific critiques citing the criterion and passage.

19
00:00:59.108 --> 00:01:01.400
Also alert on non completion rate.

20
00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.700
Should this have been multi-agent at all?

21
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.333
Probably not at first.

22
00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:12.233
One agent with a reflection step gets most of the quality, with no coordination failure.

23
00:01:12.533 --> 00:01:17.700
Multi-agent earns its keep when roles need genuinely different tools or context.

24
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.133
The trap is polishing the reviewer's prompt.

25
00:01:21.433 --> 00:01:24.367
Termination is control flow, so put it in code.

26
00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:26.290
Let's recap.

27
00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:28.700
Loops fail without a definition of done.

28
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Add a rubric, an iteration cap, and a token budget.

29
00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.833
Alert on non completion.

30
00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:37.029
And consider a single agent with reflection.

31
00:01:37.029 --> 00:01:39.200
Next up: the AI strategy meeting.
